---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { PUBLIC_COMPANY_NAME, PUBLIC_EMAIL, PUBLIC_PHONE, WHATSAPP_URL } from '../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Notice & Contact Information" description="How the contact form creates email and WhatsApp drafts, what you choose to include in an inquiry, and whom to contact about your information.">
  <article class="procurement-page procurement-privacy">
    <section class="procurement-hero"><div class="container procurement-privacy-wrap"><p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Privacy</p><h1>Privacy notice</h1></div></section>
    <div class="container procurement-privacy-wrap procurement-privacy-body">
      <p>Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-14">14 October 2026</time>. This notice describes the website's inquiry-draft feature and business contact options.</p>
      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-drafts"><h2 id="privacy-drafts">Creating an inquiry draft</h2><p>When you select <strong>Prepare inquiry</strong>, the <a href="/contact/#inquiry-form">contact form</a> creates a message in your browser. Review it, then choose <strong>Open email draft</strong> or <strong>Open WhatsApp draft</strong>. The form itself does not send the message to this website or upload attachments.</p><p>Add any files in your chosen app and send the message there. Email drafts are addressed to <a href={`mailto:${PUBLIC_EMAIL}`}>{PUBLIC_EMAIL}</a>, and WhatsApp drafts to {PUBLIC_PHONE}. Your app and its provider handle the message under their own terms.</p></section>
      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-message"><h2 id="privacy-message">Information you include</h2><p>The draft form asks for your name, destination country and either an email address or a phone number, depending on your chosen contact method. A message is optional. Product or guide references may be included when you follow an inquiry link. You can review and edit the draft before sending it.</p><p>The website does not save these form entries to its server or browser storage. Opening a draft passes its contents to the selected email app or WhatsApp service; those services may process the draft before you send it. Copying a draft places its text on your device's clipboard. Add attachments only in your chosen app, and include only the information needed for your inquiry.</p></section>
      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-technical"><h2 id="privacy-technical">Website requests and cookies</h2><p>Loading a page sends technical information, such as an IP address and browser request details, to the website's hosting infrastructure. Hosting providers may keep access or security logs. This site's current application does not set analytics or advertising cookies or include analytics and advertising trackers.</p><p>External services, including WhatsApp and your email provider, have their own privacy and storage practices. Ask the business contact below about the handling and retention of correspondence you send, including any sharing with suppliers or service providers.</p></section>
      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-business"><h2 id="privacy-business">Business contact</h2><p>Business contact: {PUBLIC_COMPANY_NAME} See the <a href="/about/#supplier-records">company page</a> for business identity and address details.</p><p>Email <a href={`mailto:${PUBLIC_EMAIL}`}>{PUBLIC_EMAIL}</a> or contact <a href={WHATSAPP_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WhatsApp · {PUBLIC_PHONE}</a>.</p></section>
      <section aria-labelledby="privacy-questions"><h2 id="privacy-questions">Questions about your information</h2><p>Write to <a href={`mailto:${PUBLIC_EMAIL}`}>{PUBLIC_EMAIL}</a> to ask how your correspondence is used or retained, request correction or deletion, or ask to stop follow-up messages.</p></section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
